{
  "id": "VA-HB-215-2026",
  "scope": "state:va",
  "title": "HB 215 (2026 Regular Session (LIS session code 20261)): Voter registration; list maintenance, third-party data exchanges approved by State Bd. of Elections.",
  "urls": [
    "https://lis.virginia.gov/bill-details/20261/HB215",
    "https://lis.virginia.gov/bill-details/20261/HB215",
    "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1225181.HTML",
    "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1219906.HTML (reenrolled 4/22/2026; not read)",
    "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1219273.HTML (Governor recommendation 4/11/2026; not read)",
    "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1199747.HTML (enrolled 3/11/2026; not read)",
    "https://lis.blob.core.windows.net/files/1083113.HTML (introduced 1/7/2026; not read)"
  ],
  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) § 24.2-404 A 4 (existing text reprinted in the act, not marked as changed)\n(quote) 4. Require the general registrars to delete from the record of registered voters the name of any voter who (i) is deceased, (ii) is no longer qualified to vote in the county or city where he is registered due to removal of his residence, (iii) has been convicted of a felony, (iv) has been adjudicated incapacitated, (v) is known not to be a United States citizen by reason of reports from the Department of Motor Vehicles pursuant to § 24.2-410.1 or from the Department of Elections based on information received from the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements Program (SAVE Program) pursuant to subsection E, or (vi) is otherwise no longer qualified to vote as may be provided by law. Such action shall be taken no later than 30 days after notification from the Department. The Department shall promptly provide the information referred to in this subdivision, upon receiving it, to general registrars.\n(section) § 24.2-404 E (existing text reprinted in the act, not marked as changed)\n(quote) E. The Department shall apply to participate in the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements Program (SAVE Program) operated by U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security for the purposes of verifying that voters listed in the Virginia voter registration system are United States citizens. Upon approval of the application, the Department shall enter into any required memorandum of agreement with U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. The State Board shall promulgate rules and regulations governing the use of the immigration status and citizenship status information received from the SAVE Program.\n(other) § 24.2-404 G (new): State Board review and two-thirds approval of memoranda of understanding for exchange of voter registration data with third parties\n(other) Enactment clause 2: Commissioner of Elections to apply for membership in the Electronic Registration Information Center (ERIC)\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
  "sponsors": [
    {
      "name": "Henson",
      "role": "author",
      "version": "Chaptered: Acts of Assembly Chapter 1038, approved 4/22/2026 (after Governor recommendation adopted)"
    }
  ],
  "single_subject": [],
